Vendor credential patterns
--------------------------

The second tier of vendor prefixes in `pkg/pii/patterns_secret.go`
(`vendorPrefixes`) is derived from the rule catalogue of betterleaks
(https://github.com/betterleaks/betterleaks), itself a fork of gitleaks, which
is licensed under the MIT License.

What is reused is the set of documented vendor token prefixes and the lengths
each vendor issues -- facts about other companies' credential formats, gathered
there and verifiable against each vendor's own documentation. The expressions
were rewritten for this engine rather than copied: RE2 rather than a boundary
assertion, no case folding over a literal prefix, and no trailing group that
consumes a character. The rules that identify a credential by the *name* beside
it, rather than by the value, are not reused at all -- this engine already reads
that shape.

